  "_note": "Hand-authored from the live deck at http://127.0.0.1:3015 (captured 2026-08-17; see vocabulary.json for the extracted shape/token baseline of the SAME capture). Models the E1 seed migration's exact local triple — hipfire GPU 0, lemonade GPU 1, comfyui GPU 1, policy_defaults verified against live /api/nodes — plus the sparky node-agent's declared sglang-omni engine, so R9's four engine-kinds (comfyui/hipfire/lemonade local_capable, sglang-omni remote_capable-only) have a REAL node-agent entry behind them, not just a catalog line: without it, no later gate item can exercise kindsFor()'s remote-vs-local split. R10: sparky's real LAN address is redacted here to 192.0.2.15 (RFC 5737 TEST-NET-1), the range .env.example's node-agent example already committed to (43112ff7) — same convention, not a new one; the real address never appears in this file or its history. GET /api/state and GET /api/storage/state carry repeat:true (R7 — POLL_MS=3000 re-fetches both every tick; Task 4 found this the hard way). GET /api/sets is fetched once on mount (SetStrip.tsx:27,36) and is NOT re-scripted. GET /api/engine-kinds carries repeat:true (Task 6 correction, discovered the hard way exactly like R7/R8: App.tsx:137-147 fetches it once on mount, but NodesView.tsx's EnginesSection ALSO fetches it independently on every mount of a node's Engines editor (reload(), fired again by useEffect(reload, [nodeId]) on every rail-row selection) — a single-entry, non-repeat script exhausts on the SECOND fetch and 599s the whole editor into 'Could not load engines' before any of E1 items 1-3 can render. The kinds payload never changes within a run, so repeat is correct here, not a workaround. GET /api/nodes, POST .../engines, DELETE .../engines/{resource}, and GET /api/policy are scripted exactly to Task 7's needs: nodes goes triple -> triple+gguf-test -> back to triple (declare, then forget); policy goes 3 rows -> 4 rows. gguf-test is deliberately GPU 1 + pinned:true — both AWAY from the add-form's defaults (GPU 0 is the picker's first option; DEFAULT_POLICY.pinned is false, model/engineForm.ts) — so a form that silently dropped the operator's picks would still fail a gpu_index:0/pinned:false assertion instead of coinciding with it.",
